Chapter: Over Apply Partial
  cites Codex chapter Text

 Probe for Lesson 2 — arity-aware over-apply. `partial` has arity 1 and
 returns a partially-applied closure of `add`. Calling `partial 10 5`
 flattens to {partial, [10, 5]}: the emitter must split — direct-call
 partial(10) → closure, indirect-call closure(5) → 15. Without the
 arity check, the emitter would call partial as if it were arity-2 and
 silently drop the 5.

 This deliberately avoids IrLambda so the test isolates the over-apply
 path — `partial` returns a named partial-application, not a `\y -> ...`.

Section: Definitions
  add : Integer -> Integer -> Integer
  add (x) (y) = x + y

  partial : Integer -> (Integer -> Integer)
  partial (n) = add n

  opening : Integer = partial 10 5

